CMake's FindOpenGL will not report OpenGL as found under the GLVND preference
unless it locates both libOpenGL and libGLX. A GBM image has no GLX at all --
the sysroot carries libOpenGL.so and libGLdispatch.so and nothing else -- so
the configure step ends at "Could NOT find OpenGL (missing: OPENGL_glx_LIBRARY)"
and the GS renderer is linked without any GL library.

The core needs GL entry points, not GLX. Most of them -- 274 of the 292 it uses
-- come from the libretro hardware-render get_proc_address at runtime and need
nothing at link time. The remaining 18 are the GL 1.x calls <GL/gl.h> declares
as ordinary functions (glEnable, glClear, glDrawArrays, glReadPixels and the
like), and those do have to resolve against a library. So when FindOpenGL fails
but libOpenGL is present, use it.

diff --git a/cmake/SearchForStuff.cmake b/cmake/SearchForStuff.cmake
index da6eba91e..14533ba60 100644
--- a/cmake/SearchForStuff.cmake
+++ b/cmake/SearchForStuff.cmake
@@ -15,6 +15,19 @@ find_package(LibLZMA)
 # is deprecated as of cmake 3.11.
 set(OpenGL_GL_PREFERENCE GLVND)
 find_package(OpenGL)
+
+# No GLX on a GBM/EGL target, which is the only thing FindOpenGL was missing.
+# libOpenGL exports the same entry points, so link that directly.
+if(NOT OPENGL_FOUND)
+    find_library(OPENGL_opengl_LIBRARY NAMES OpenGL)
+    if(OPENGL_opengl_LIBRARY)
+        set(OPENGL_FOUND TRUE)
+        set(OPENGL_LIBRARIES ${OPENGL_opengl_LIBRARY})
+        set(OPENGL_INCLUDE_DIR "")
+        message(STATUS "Using ${OPENGL_opengl_LIBRARY} directly: no GLX on this target")
+    endif()
+endif()
+
 find_package(PNG)
 set(wxWidgets_FOUND 1)
 set(wxWidgets_USE_FILE 3rdparty/wxwidgets3.0/UsewxWidgets.cmake)
